      "summary": "Leaders from the United States and Denmark have announced an agreement under which the US will take a permanent role in Greenland’s security, allowing a sustained American military presence on the island and aiming to prevent rival powers from establishing bases; Denmark characterizes the arrangement as compatible with NATO and Europe and describes security as shared, while details such as the scope, duration and basing arrangements were highlighted as key elements in reporting."
